  data: {
    LLM: "Keep your Aces for trumps. In a 24-card game, an Ace is incredibly powerful because there are only three other cards of that suit in existence.\n\nThe 'Nine' Lead: If you have no trumps, lead a 9 of a plain suit. This forces the opponent to follow suit with a potentially higher point-scoring card (like a King), which your partner may then capture with a trump.\n\nCounting the 40: Memorize the points as they fall. If you know 20 points have already been won by your side, your only goal is to secure ONE more point (the lowest Jack) to fulfill your contract.",
    Player: "Keep your Aces for trumps. In a 24-card game, an Ace is incredibly powerful because there are only three other cards of that suit in existence.\n\nThe 'Nine' Lead: If you have no trumps, lead a 9 of a plain suit. This forces the opponent to follow suit with a potentially higher point-scoring card (like a King), which your partner may then capture with a trump.\n\nCounting the 40: Memorize the points as they fall. If you know 20 points have already been won by your side, your only goal is to secure ONE more point (the lowest Jack) to fulfill your contract.",
